       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the usual maximum dose of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg aren't recommended, and they raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia without much added benefit.\n\nDid you mean 10 mg, or is there a reason for 20 mg, such as a specialist recommendation? Here are some options:\n\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose.\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily.** This is a typical starting dose, and 2.5 mg is used for frail patients or those with hepatic impairment.\n- **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** I can enter it if you confirm it's intentional, and I'll add a note documenting the rationale.\n- **A second agent.** If 10 mg isn't controlling blood pressure, adding an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-type diuretic is usually preferred over going above the maximum.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it."
      }
